From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christophe Pettus <xof@thebuild.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 12:09:56 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 26/35] H16: refuse JPEG 2000 component counts the decoder
 cannot hold

Two crafted shapes panicked inside hayro-jpeg2000 at any memory budget.

With palette indices unresolved (as hayro-syntax decodes), a JP2 file
with a pclr box is decoded as one gray index channel, and the
component-count check is skipped for palette images, so a codestream of
two or more components was interleaved past the end of the one-channel
output buffer. Such a file is now refused with TooManyChannels.

The progression iterator narrows the component count to a u8, so 256
components became 0 (a failed assertion) and 257 became 1 (components
silently dropped). Raw codestreams were already refused by the channel
check; JP2 files with a palette were not. Any count above 255 is now
refused with TooManyChannels in resolve_alpha_and_color_space, the one
function every Image is built through, before any decoding.

hayro-syntax reports both refusals as ImageDecode, so the image is
skipped with an image-decode warning.

Refs internal #63
---
 hayro-jpeg2000/src/lib.rs | 15 +++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 15 insertions(+)

diff --git a/hayro-jpeg2000/src/lib.rs b/hayro-jpeg2000/src/lib.rs
index 43c6202..8800792 100644
--- a/hayro-jpeg2000/src/lib.rs
+++ b/hayro-jpeg2000/src/lib.rs
@@ -293,6 +293,14 @@ pub(crate) fn resolve_alpha_and_color_space(
 ) -> Result<(ColorSpace, bool)> {
     let mut num_components = header.component_infos.len();
 
+    // The decoder keeps component counts in a `u8` (the progression
+    // iterator narrows to one), so more than 255 would truncate. Every
+    // `Image` is built through here, so refusing it here covers raw
+    // codestreams and JP2 files alike, before any decoding.
+    if num_components > u8::MAX as usize {
+        bail!(ValidationError::TooManyChannels);
+    }
+
     // Override number of components with what is actually in the palette box
     // in case we resolve them.
     if settings.resolve_palette_indices
@@ -318,6 +326,13 @@ pub(crate) fn resolve_alpha_and_color_space(
 
     let actual_num_components = header.component_infos.len();
 
+    // Unresolved, the output holds one index channel per pixel, so a
+    // palette image with more components would be interleaved past its end
+    // (the channel check below skips palette images).
+    if !settings.resolve_palette_indices && boxes.palette.is_some() && actual_num_components != 1 {
+        bail!(ValidationError::TooManyChannels);
+    }
+
     // Validate the number of channels.
     if boxes.palette.is_none()
         && actual_num_components
